{"id":"mahabharata-2-061","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":61,"title":"एकषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 61 · Vikarna's protest and Draupadi's disrobing","summary":{"en":"Bhima wants to burn Yudhishthira's hands and is restrained by Arjuna. Young Vikarna declares Draupadi was not lawfully won, but Karna silences him and orders the Pandavas and Draupadi stripped; when Duhshasana pulls at her garment, more and more garments appear in its place, and Bhima vows to drink Duhshasana's blood.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನ ಕೈಗಳನ್ನು ಸುಡಲು ಬಯಸಿದ ಭೀಮನನ್ನು ಅರ್ಜುನನು ತಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯನ್ನು ನ್ಯಾಯವಾಗಿ ಗೆಲ್ಲಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ಯುವಕ ವಿಕರ್ಣನು ಘೋಷಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಕರ್ಣನು ಅವನ ಬಾಯಿ ಮುಚ್ಚಿಸಿ ಪಾಂಡವರ ಮತ್ತು ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯ ವಸ್ತ್ರ ಸೆಳೆಯಲು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದುಃಶಾಸನನು ಸೀರೆ ಎಳೆದಂತೆ ಅದರ ಸ್ಥಾನದಲ್ಲಿ ಮತ್ತೆ ಮತ್ತೆ ವಸ್ತ್ರಗಳು ಕಾಣಿಸುತ್ತವೆ; ದುಃಶಾಸನನ ರಕ್ತ ಕುಡಿಯುವೆನೆಂದು ಭೀಮನು ಪ್ರತಿಜ್ಞೆ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीम युधिष्ठिर के हाथ जलाना चाहते हैं और अर्जुन उन्हें रोकते हैं। युवा विकर्ण घोषणा करता है कि द्रौपदी न्याय से नहीं जीती गई, पर कर्ण उसे चुप कराकर पाण्डवों और द्रौपदी के वस्त्र उतारने का आदेश देते हैं; जब दुःशासन उनका वस्त्र खींचता है, उसके स्थान पर और वस्त्र प्रकट होते जाते हैं, और भीम दुःशासन का रक्त पीने की प्रतिज्ञा करते हैं।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుని చేతులను కాల్చాలనుకున్న భీముని అర్జునుడు నివారిస్తాడు. ద్రౌపదిని న్యాయంగా గెలవలేదని యువకుడు వికర్ణుడు ప్రకటిస్తాడు, కర్ణుడు అతని నోరు మూయించి పాండవుల, ద్రౌపది వస్త్రాలు లాగమంటాడు; దుశ్శాసనుడు చీర లాగుతుండగా దాని స్థానంలో మళ్లీ మళ్లీ వస్త్రాలు ప్రత్యక్షమవుతాయి; దుశ్శాసనుని రక్తం తాగుతానని భీముడు ప్రతిజ్ఞ చేస్తాడు.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரரின் கைகளை எரிக்க விரும்பிய பீமனை அர்ஜுனன் தடுக்கிறான். திரௌபதி நேர்மையாக வெல்லப்படவில்லை என்று இளைஞன் விகர்ணன் அறிவிக்க, கர்ணன் அவனை அடக்கிப் பாண்டவர்கள், திரௌபதியின் ஆடைகளைக் களையச் சொல்கிறான்; துச்ஶாஸனன் அவள் ஆடையை இழுக்க இழுக்க அதன் இடத்தில் மேலும் மேலும் ஆடைகள் தோன்றுகின்றன; துச்ஶாஸனனின் ரத்தத்தைக் குடிப்பதாகப் பீமன் சபதம் செய்கிறான்.","ml":"യുധിഷ്ഠിരന്റെ കൈകൾ ചുട്ടുകളയാൻ ഭീമൻ ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്നു; അർജുനൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ തടയുന്നു. യുവാവായ വികർണ്ണൻ ദ്രൗപദിയെ ന്യായമായി നേടിയതല്ലെന്ന് പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു; എന്നാൽ കർണ്ണൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ നിശ്ശബ്ദനാക്കി, പാണ്ഡവരെയും ദ്രൗപദിയെയും വസ്ത്രം അഴിക്കാൻ കല്പിക്കുന്നു. ദുശ്ശാസനൻ അവളുടെ വസ്ത്രം വലിക്കുമ്പോൾ, അതിന് പകരമായി കൂടുതൽ കൂടുതൽ വസ്ത്രങ്ങൾ പ്രത്യക്ഷപ്പെടുന്നു; ദുശ്ശാസനന്റെ രക്തം കുടിക്കുമെന്ന് ഭീമൻ പ്രതിജ്ഞയെടുക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.61; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"द्यूतपर्व","titleEn":"Dyuta Parva (The dice game)","verses":[{"text":"भीम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhima said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भवन्ति देशे बन्धक्यः कितवानां युधिष्ठिर ।\nन ताभिरुत दीव्यन्ति दया चैवास्ति तास्वपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, in some lands gamblers keep courtesans, and even they do not gamble them away; there is some mercy even toward them."}},{"n":2,"text":"काश्यो यद्बलिमाहार्षीद्द्रव्यं यच्चान्यदुत्तमम् ।\nतथान्ये पृथिवीपाला यानि रत्नान्युपाहरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The tribute the king of Kashi brought and the other fine goods, and the jewels the other kings offered,"}},{"n":3,"text":"वाहनानि धनं चैव कवचान्यायुधानि च ।\nराज्यमात्मा वयं चैव कैतवेन हृतं परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vehicles, wealth, armor and weapons, the kingdom, ourselves and you, were all taken by our enemies through cheating."}},{"n":4,"text":"न च मे तत्र कोपोऽभूत्सर्वस्येशो हि नो भवान् ।\nइदं त्वतिकृतं मन्ये द्रौपदी यत्र पण्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I felt no anger at that, for you are master of us all. But I think this is the limit, that Draupadi was staked."}},{"n":5,"text":"एषा ह्यनर्हती बाला पाण्डवान्प्राप्य कौरवैः ।\nत्वत्कृते क्लिश्यते क्षुद्रैर्नृशंसैर्निकृतिप्रियैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This young woman, who did not deserve it, has come to the Pandavas and is tormented by the Kauravas, petty, cruel, lovers of cheating, because of you."}},{"n":6,"text":"अस्याः कृते मन्युरयं त्वयि राजन्निपात्यते ।\nबाहू ते संप्रधक्ष्यामि सहदेवाग्निमानय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because of her, king, this anger of mine falls on you. I will burn your arms. Sahadeva, bring fire."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"न पुरा भीमसेन त्वमीदृशीर्वदिता गिरः ।\nपरैस्ते नाशितं नूनं नृशंसैर्धर्मगौरवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, you never spoke such words before. Surely the cruel enemies have destroyed your respect for dharma."}},{"n":8,"text":"न सकामाः परे कार्या धर्ममेवाचरोत्तमम् ।\nभ्रातरं धार्मिकं ज्येष्ठं नातिक्रमितुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"We must not fulfill the enemy's wishes; practice the highest dharma. One should not transgress against one's righteous eldest brother."}},{"n":9,"text":"आहूतो हि परै राजा क्षात्रधर्ममनुस्मरन् ।\nदीव्यते परकामेन तन्नः कीर्तिकरं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When challenged by enemies, the king, remembering the kshatriya law, played at their wish. That brings us great renown."}},{"text":"भीमसेन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"एवमस्मिकृतं विद्यां यद्यस्याहं धनंजय ।\nदीप्तेऽग्नौ सहितौ बाहू निर्दहेयं बलादिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya, if I knew that this was so done to him, I would burn his joined arms by force in a blazing fire."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"तथा तान्दुःखितान्दृष्ट्वा पाण्डवान्धृतराष्ट्रजः ।\nक्लिश्यमानां च पाञ्चालीं विकर्ण इदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Pandavas in such grief and Panchali in torment, Vikarna, son of Dhritarashtra, spoke."}},{"n":12,"text":"याज्ञसेन्या यदुक्तं तद्वाक्यं विब्रूत पार्थिवाः ।\nअविवेकेन वाक्यस्य नरकः सद्य एव नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings, say what Yajnasena's daughter asked. If we fail to give the right answer, we go to hell at once."}},{"n":13,"text":"भीष्मश्च धृतराष्ट्रश्च कुरुवृद्धतमावुभौ ।\nसमेत्य नाहतुः किंचिद्विदुरश्च महामतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma and Dhritarashtra, the eldest of the Kurus, both met together and said nothing, and neither did the greatly wise Vidura."}},{"n":14,"text":"भारद्वाजोऽपि सर्वेषामाचार्यः कृप एव च ।\nअत एतावपि प्रश्नं नाहतुर्द्विजसत्तमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharadvaja's son Drona, teacher of all, and Kripa, those two best of brahmins, also did not answer the question."}},{"n":15,"text":"ये त्वन्ये पृथिवीपालाः समेताः सर्वतो दिशः ।\nकामक्रोधौ समुत्सृज्य ते ब्रुवन्तु यथामति ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the other kings gathered from every direction, let them cast off desire and anger and speak as they think."}},{"n":16,"text":"यदिदं द्रौपदी वाक्यमुक्तवत्यसकृच्छुभा ।\nविमृश्य कस्य कः पक्षः पार्थिवा वदतोत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Consider what the fair Draupadi has said again and again; kings, say whose side each of you is on and give an answer."}},{"n":17,"text":"एवं स बहुशः सर्वानुक्तवांस्तान्सभासदः ।\nन च ते पृथिवीपालास्तमूचुः साध्वसाधु वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"So he spoke many times to all the assembly members, but those kings said to him nothing, good or bad."}},{"n":18,"text":"उक्त्वा तथासकृत्सर्वान्विकर्णः पृथिवीपतीन् ।\nपाणिं पाणौ विनिष्पिष्य निःश्वसन्निदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having addressed all the kings many times, Vikarna, rubbing hand against hand and sighing, said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"विब्रूत पृथिवीपाला वाक्यं मा वा कथंचन ।\nमन्ये न्याय्यं यदत्राहं तद्धि वक्ष्यामि कौरवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings, speak or do not speak at all. I will say what I consider just here, Kauravas."}},{"n":20,"text":"चत्वार्याहुर्नरश्रेष्ठा व्यसनानि महीक्षिताम् ।\nमृगयां पानमक्षांश्च ग्राम्ये चैवातिसक्तताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of men, they say there are four vices of kings: hunting, drinking, dice, and excessive attachment to women."}},{"n":21,"text":"एतेषु हि नरः सक्तो धर्ममुत्सृज्य वर्तते ।\nतथायुक्तेन च कृतां क्रियां लोको न मन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man addicted to these leaves dharma and acts; and the world does not accept what a man in such a state has done."}},{"n":22,"text":"तदयं पाण्डुपुत्रेण व्यसने वर्तता भृशम् ।\nसमाहूतेन कितवैरास्थितो द्रौपदीपणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This Pandava, deep in vice, called by gamblers, wagered Draupadi."}},{"n":23,"text":"साधारणी च सर्वेषां पाण्डवानामनिन्दिता ।\nजितेन पूर्वं चानेन पाण्डवेन कृतः पणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That blameless one was common to all the Pandavas, and this Pandava made the stake after having lost himself."}},{"n":24,"text":"इयं च कीर्तिता कृष्णा सौबलेन पणार्थिना ।\nएतत्सर्वं विचार्याहं मन्ये न विजितामिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And this Krishna was named by Subala's son, who wanted stakes. Considering all this, I think she has not been won."}},{"n":25,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा महान्नादः सभ्यानामुदतिष्ठत ।\nविकर्णं शंसमानानां सौबलं च विनिन्दताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, a great uproar rose among the assembly, praising Vikarna and condemning Shakuni."}},{"n":26,"text":"तस्मिन्नुपरते शब्दे राधेयः क्रोधमूर्छितः ।\nप्रगृह्य रुचिरं बाहुमिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the noise stopped, Karna, Radha's son, benumbed with anger, raised his fine arm and said this."}},{"n":27,"text":"दृश्यन्ते वै विकर्णे हि वैकृतानि बहून्यपि ।\nतज्जस्तस्य विनाशाय यथाग्निररणिप्रजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many signs of perversity are seen in Vikarna, born to bring his destruction, as fire is born of the fire-drill."}},{"n":28,"text":"एते न किंचिदप्याहुश्चोद्यमानापि कृष्णया ।\nधर्मेण विजितां मन्ये मन्यन्ते द्रुपदात्मजाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though urged by Krishna, these others say nothing. I think they hold that Drupada's daughter was won by right."}},{"n":29,"text":"त्वं तु केवलबाल्येन धार्तराष्ट्र विदीर्यसे ।\nयद्ब्रवीषि सभामध्ये बालः स्थविरभाषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Dhritarashtra, you are torn by sheer childishness, since in the midst of the assembly, a boy, you speak like an elder."}},{"n":30,"text":"न च धर्मं यथातत्त्वं वेत्सि दुर्योधनावर ।\nयद्ब्रवीषि जितां कृष्णामजितेति सुमन्दधीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Youngest of Duryodhana's brothers, you do not know dharma as it is, dull-witted, when you say Krishna was not won though she was."}},{"n":31,"text":"कथं ह्यविजितां कृष्णां मन्यसे धृतराष्ट्रज ।\nयदा सभायां सर्वस्वं न्यस्तवान्पाण्डवाग्रजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can you think Krishna not won, son of Dhritarashtra, when the Pandava's elder brother staked everything in the hall?"}},{"n":32,"text":"अभ्यन्तरा च सर्वस्वे द्रौपदी भरतर्षभ ।\nएवं धर्मजितां कृष्णां मन्यसे न जितां कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Draupadi, bull of the Bharatas, was included in everything; how can you think the one won by dharma was not won?"}},{"n":33,"text":"कीर्तिता द्रौपदी वाचा अनुज्ञाता च पाण्डवैः ।\nभवत्यविजिता केन हेतुनैषा मता तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi was named by his voice and permitted by the Pandavas; for what reason do you think she is not won?"}},{"n":34,"text":"मन्यसे वा सभामेतामानीतामेकवाससम् ।\nअधर्मेणेति तत्रापि शृणु मे वाक्यमुत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or you may think she was brought to this hall in a single garment unrighteously; hear my answer to that too."}},{"n":35,"text":"एको भर्ता स्त्रिया देवैर्विहितः कुरुनन्दन ।\nइयं त्वनेकवशगा बन्धकीति विनिश्चिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods ordained one husband for a woman, delight of the Kurus; she who goes under many is fixed as a courtesan."}},{"n":36,"text":"अस्याः सभामानयनं न चित्रमिति मे मतिः ।\nएकाम्बरधरत्वं वाप्यथ वापि विवस्त्रता ॥","meaning":{"en":"So bringing her into the assembly is no wonder, I think, nor her being in one garment or even naked."}},{"n":37,"text":"यच्चैषां द्रविणं किंचिद्या चैषा ये च पाण्डवाः ।\nसौबलेनेह तत्सर्वं धर्मेण विजितं वसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever wealth they had, and she, and the Pandavas themselves, all that was rightly won by Subala's son."}},{"n":38,"text":"दुःशासन सुबालोऽयं विकर्णः प्राज्ञवादिकः ।\nपाण्डवानां च वासांसि द्रौपद्याश्चाप्युपाहर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duhshasana, this Vikarna is a child who speaks like a wise man. Take off the Pandavas' garments and Draupadi's too."}},{"n":39,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा पाण्डवाः सर्वे स्वानि वासांसि भारत ।\nअवकीर्योत्तरीयाणि सभायां समुपाविशन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that, all the Pandavas took off their upper garments and sat down in the assembly."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततो दुःशासनो राजन्द्रौपद्या वसनं बलात् ।\nसभामध्ये समाक्षिप्य व्यपक्रष्टुं प्रचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duhshasana, king, seized Draupadi's garment by force in the midst of the hall and began to pull it away."}},{"n":41,"text":"आकृष्यमाणे वसने द्रौपद्यास्तु विशां पते ।\nतद्रूपमपरं वस्त्रं प्रादुरासीदनेकशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Draupadi's garment was pulled, lord of the people, another garment just like it appeared again and again, many times."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततो हलहलाशब्दस्तत्रासीद्घोरनिस्वनः ।\nतदद्भुततमं लोके वीक्ष्य सर्वमहीक्षिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a terrible tumult of shouting arose there, as all the kings saw that most wondrous thing in the world."}},{"n":43,"text":"शशाप तत्र भीमस्तु राजमध्ये महास्वनः ।\nक्रोधाद्विस्फुरमाणोष्ठो विनिष्पिष्य करे करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, roaring in the midst of the kings, lips quivering with anger, rubbing hand against hand, uttered an oath."}},{"n":44,"text":"इदं मे वाक्यमादद्ध्वं क्षत्रिया लोकवासिनः ।\nनोक्तपूर्वं नरैरन्यैर्न चान्यो यद्वदिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kshatriyas of the world, hear this word of mine, which no other men have said before and none will say after."}},{"n":45,"text":"यद्येतदेवमुक्त्वा तु न कुर्यां पृथिवीश्वराः ।\nपितामहानां सर्वेषां नाहं गतिमवाप्नुयाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I do not do what I say, lords of the earth, may I not reach the destination of all my forefathers."}},{"n":46,"text":"अस्य पापस्य दुर्जातेर्भारतापसदस्य च ।\nन पिबेयं बलाद्वक्षो भित्त्वा चेद्रुधिरं युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I do not tear open the chest of this wicked, ill-born disgrace of the Bharatas in battle and drink his blood by force, may I not."}},{"n":47,"text":"तस्य ते वचनं श्रुत्वा सर्वलोकप्रहर्षणम् ।\nप्रचक्रुर्बहुलां पूजां कुत्सन्तो धृतराष्ट्रजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, which thrilled the whole world, they gave great honor to Bhima and condemned the son of Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":48,"text":"यदा तु वाससां राशिः सभामध्ये समाचितः ।\nततो दुःशासनः श्रान्तो व्रीडितः समुपाविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a pile of garments had heaped up in the middle of the hall, Duhshasana, weary and ashamed, sat down."}},{"n":49,"text":"धिक्शब्दस्तु ततस्तत्र समभूल्लोमहर्षणः ।\nसभ्यानां नरदेवानां दृष्ट्वा कुन्तीसुतांस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a hair-raising cry of Shame! arose from the assembled kings as they looked at the sons of Kunti."}},{"n":50,"text":"न विब्रुवन्ति कौरव्याः प्रश्नमेतमिति स्म ह ।\nस जनः क्रोशति स्मात्र धृतराष्ट्रं विगर्हयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kauravas gave no answer to that question, and the people there cried out, blaming Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":51,"text":"ततो बाहू समुच्छ्रित्य निवार्य च सभासदः ।\nविदुरः सर्वधर्मज्ञ इदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vidura, who knew all dharma, raised his arms and silenced the assembly and said this."}},{"text":"विदुर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vidura said:"}},{"n":52,"text":"द्रौपदी प्रश्नमुक्त्वैवं रोरवीति ह्यनाथवत् ।\nन च विब्रूत तं प्रश्नं सभ्या धर्मोऽत्र पीड्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi, having put her question, cries like one without protectors. You do not answer, assembly members; dharma is being afflicted here."}},{"n":53,"text":"सभां प्रपद्यते ह्यार्तः प्रज्वलन्निव हव्यवाट् ।\nतं वै सत्येन धर्मेण सभ्याः प्रशमयन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"A distressed person comes to the assembly like a blazing fire; the assembly members calm it with truth and dharma."}},{"n":54,"text":"धर्मप्रश्नमथो ब्रूयादार्तः सभ्येषु मानवः ।\nविब्रूयुस्तत्र ते प्रश्नं कामक्रोधवशातिगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man in distress may put a question of dharma to the assembly; those who are free of desire and anger should answer it."}},{"n":55,"text":"विकर्णेन यथाप्रज्ञमुक्तः प्रश्नो नराधिपाः ।\nभवन्तोऽपि हि तं प्रश्नं विब्रुवन्तु यथामति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vikarna, kings, has answered the question as he understood it. You too should answer it according to your understanding."}},{"n":56,"text":"यो हि प्रश्नं न विब्रूयाद्धर्मदर्शी सभां गतः ।\nअनृते या फलावाप्तिस्तस्याः सोऽर्धं समश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"An assembly member who sees dharma but does not answer the question when he is in the hall shares half the fruit of any falsehood."}},{"n":57,"text":"यः पुनर्वितथं ब्रूयाद्धर्मदर्शी सभां गतः ।\nअनृतस्य फलं कृत्स्नं संप्राप्नोतीति निश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But one who sees dharma and speaks falsely in the hall gets the whole fruit of the lie: this is certain."}},{"n":58,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nप्रह्लादस्य च संवादं मुनेराङ्गिरसस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this they recount an ancient tale, the conversation of Prahlada and the sage Angirasa's son."}},{"n":59,"text":"प्रह्लादो नाम दैत्येन्द्रस्तस्य पुत्रो विरोचनः ।\nकन्याहेतोराङ्गिरसं सुधन्वानमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prahlada was lord of the Daityas; his son Virochana went to Sudhanvan, Angirasa's son, over a girl."}},{"n":60,"text":"अहं ज्यायानहं ज्यायानिति कन्येप्सया तदा ।\nतयोर्देवनमत्रासीत्प्राणयोरिति नः श्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each said, I am greater, I am greater, desiring the maiden, and we hear that they wagered their lives on it."}},{"n":61,"text":"तयोः प्रश्नविवादोऽभूत्प्रह्लादं तावपृच्छताम् ।\nज्यायान्क आवयोरेकः प्रश्नं प्रब्रूहि मा मृषा ॥","meaning":{"en":"They disputed over a question, and asked Prahlada: Which of us is greater? Answer the question, and do not lie."}},{"n":62,"text":"स वै विवदनाद्भीतः सुधन्वानं व्यलोकयत् ।\nतं सुधन्वाब्रवीत्क्रुद्धो ब्रह्मदण्ड इव ज्वलन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Afraid of the dispute, Prahlada looked at Sudhanvan, who, angry and blazing like a brahmin's curse-rod, said to him:"}},{"n":63,"text":"यदि वै वक्ष्यसि मृषा प्रह्लादाथ न वक्ष्यसि ।\nशतधा ते शिरो वज्री वज्रेण प्रहरिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you speak falsely, Prahlada, or if you do not speak, the wielder of the thunderbolt will strike your head with his bolt into a hundred pieces."}},{"n":64,"text":"सुधन्वना तथोक्तः सन्व्यथितोऽश्वत्थपर्णवत् ।\nजगाम कश्यपं दैत्यः परिप्रष्टुं महौजसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by Sudhanvan, the Daitya trembled like a peepal leaf and went to question the greatly energetic Kashyapa."}},{"text":"प्रह्लाद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Prahlada said:"}},{"n":65,"text":"त्वं वै धर्मस्य विज्ञाता दैवस्येहासुरस्य च ।\nब्राह्मणस्य महाप्राज्ञ धर्मकृच्छ्रमिदं शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"You know the dharma of gods, of asuras, and of brahmins, wise one; hear this difficulty of dharma."}},{"n":66,"text":"यो वै प्रश्नं न विब्रूयाद्वितथं वापि निर्दिशेत् ।\nके वै तस्य परे लोकास्तन्ममाचक्ष्व पृच्छतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What worlds in the next life does one have who does not answer a question, or who answers falsely? Tell me, who ask."}},{"text":"कश्यप उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kashyapa said:"}},{"n":67,"text":"जानन्न विब्रुवन्प्रश्नं कामात्क्रोधात्तथा भयात् ।\nसहस्रं वारुणान्पाशानात्मनि प्रतिमुञ्चति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who knows the answer but does not give it, out of desire, anger or fear, binds himself with a thousand nooses of Varuna."}},{"n":68,"text":"तस्य संवत्सरे पूर्णे पाश एकः प्रमुच्यते ।\nतस्मात्सत्यं तु वक्तव्यं जानता सत्यमञ्जसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a full year has passed, one noose is loosened for him. Therefore one who knows should speak the truth plainly."}},{"n":69,"text":"विद्धो धर्मो ह्यधर्मेण सभां यत्र प्रपद्यते ।\nन चास्य शल्यं कृन्तन्ति विद्धास्तत्र सभासदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where dharma comes to an assembly pierced by adharma, and the members do not remove the arrow, they themselves are pierced."}},{"n":70,"text":"अर्धं हरति वै श्रेष्ठः पादो भवति कर्तृषु ।\nपादश्चैव सभासत्सु ये न निन्दन्ति निन्दितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The chief takes half the guilt, a quarter goes to the doers, and a quarter to the assembly members who do not blame what is blameworthy."}},{"n":71,"text":"अनेना भवति श्रेष्ठो मुच्यन्ते च सभासदः ।\nएनो गच्छति कर्तारं निन्दार्हो यत्र निन्द्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The chief is blameless and the members are freed when blame falls on the doer where blame is due."}},{"n":72,"text":"वितथं तु वदेयुर्ये धर्मं प्रह्लाद पृच्छते ।\nइष्टापूर्तं च ते घ्नन्ति सप्त चैव परावरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But those who answer falsely to one asking about dharma, Prahlada, destroy their sacrifices and good works and seven generations before and after."}},{"n":73,"text":"हृतस्वस्य हि यद्दुःखं हतपुत्रस्य चापि यत् ।\nऋणिनं प्रति यच्चैव राज्ञा ग्रस्तस्य चापि यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sorrow of one robbed of his wealth, of one who has lost a son, of a debtor, of one seized by a king,"}},{"n":74,"text":"स्त्रियाः पत्या विहीनायाः सार्थाद्भ्रष्टस्य चैव यत् ।\nअध्यूढायाश्च यद्दुःखं साक्षिभिर्विहतस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of a woman without a husband, of one separated from his caravan, of a woman whose co-wife rules, and of one ruined by witnesses,"}},{"n":75,"text":"एतानि वै समान्याहुर्दुःखानि त्रिदशेश्वराः ।\nतानि सर्वाणि दुःखानि प्राप्नोति वितथं ब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lords of the gods say these sorrows are alike; one who speaks falsely gets all those sorrows."}},{"n":76,"text":"समक्षदर्शनात्साक्ष्यं श्रवणाच्चेति धारणात् ।\nतस्मात्सत्यं ब्रुवन्साक्षी धर्मार्थाभ्यां न हीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A witness is one who tells what he saw directly, heard, and retained; so a witness who speaks the truth is not deprived of dharma and wealth."}},{"text":"विदुर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vidura said:"}},{"n":77,"text":"कश्यपस्य वचः श्रुत्वा प्रह्लादः पुत्रमब्रवीत् ।\nश्रेयान्सुधन्वा त्वत्तो वै मत्तः श्रेयांस्तथाङ्गिराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Kashyapa's words, Prahlada said to his son: Sudhanvan is better than you, and Angirasa is better than I."}},{"n":78,"text":"माता सुधन्वनश्चापि श्रेयसी मातृतस्तव ।\nविरोचन सुधन्वायं प्राणानामीश्वरस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Sudhanvan's mother is better than your mother. So, Virochana, this Sudhanvan is master of your life."}},{"text":"सुधन्वोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sudhanvan said:"}},{"n":79,"text":"पुत्रस्नेहं परित्यज्य यस्त्वं धर्मे प्रतिष्ठितः ।\nअनुजानामि ते पुत्रं जीवत्वेष शतं समाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since you, set in dharma, have put aside love for your son, I grant that your son shall live a hundred years."}},{"text":"विदुर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vidura said:"}},{"n":80,"text":"एवं वै परमं धर्मं श्रुत्वा सर्वे सभासदः ।\nयथाप्रश्नं तु कृष्णाया मन्यध्वं तत्र किं परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard this supreme dharma, all of you in the assembly, consider what is best in answer to Krishna's question."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":81,"text":"विदुरस्य वचः श्रुत्वा नोचुः किंचन पार्थिवाः ।\nकर्णो दुःशासनं त्वाह कृष्णां दासीं गृहान्नय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Vidura's words, the kings said nothing. Karna said to Duhshasana, Take Krishna, the slave, to the house."}},{"n":82,"text":"तां वेपमानां सव्रीडां प्रलपन्तीं स्म पाण्डवान् ।\nदुःशासनः सभामध्ये विचकर्ष तपस्विनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trembling, ashamed, lamenting for the Pandavas, that ascetic-like woman was dragged by Duhshasana in the midst of the hall."}}]}]}